## Model card

- **Name:** QoDuck
- **Short description:** Local metadata describes QoDuck as a stealth coding/reasoning preview model in Qoder (suspected Qwen-family checkpoint) with adaptive thinking and large context, but accessible public sources in this pass provided no independently verifiable official model card, specs, or standardized benchmark results for this exact identity.
- **Provider / access:** Claimed as Qoder desktop/platform preview (`opencode/qoduck`, `qoder.ai`) in local metadata, with a free preview tier/allowance context. Qoder docs/navigation references “Qoduck: Try the Stealth Model Free for a Limited Time”, but detailed model specs/benchmarks were not verifiable from accessible pages in this pass.
- **Release / knowledge:** Stealth preview; release date and knowledge cutoff not publicly documented/verified.
- **IDs:** `qoduck`, `opencode/qoduck` (local/preview identifiers).
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 total tokens (65,536 max output) per local metadata claim; not independently verified from accessible official documentation in this pass.
- **Modalities:** Text and image input; text and code output per local metadata claim; not independently verified.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-14):** Free preview tier (0.0x credits) in Qoder desktop per local metadata claim; broader hosted pricing not verified from accessible official model-specific documentation.
- **Architecture:** Undisclosed/stealth. Architecture and parameter count not publicly disclosed/verified (metadata notes “suspected Qwen 4 checkpoint” as unverified speculation).

